Built with `nix build .#cloud-redirect` under `pkgs.pkgsi686Linux.stdenv`
(genuine i686 toolchain, not -m32 cross-compilation on a 64-bit compiler --
see nix-modules/default.nix). This sidesteps CMakeLists.txt's Fedora/Debian
multilib-path guessing for LINUX_32BIT entirely, since CMAKE_SIZEOF_VOID_P is
already 4 under that stdenv.

The flake is pinned to the NixOS 21.11 userspace baseline (GCC 10/glibc
2.33), and the package fixup removes its Nix-store RUNPATH before staging.

Confirmed ELF32/Intel 80386. NEEDED: libdl.so.2, libpthread.so.0,
libatomic.so.1, libstdc++.so.6, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6 and
ld-linux.so.2. Highest required glibc symbol version: GLIBC_2.33. No RPATH or
RUNPATH remains, and CloudRedirect's Linux target needs no openssl/curl.

The complete public suite passes: `test/linux_lua_discovery_tests.cpp`,
`test/linux_init_stop_tests.cpp`, and `test/manual_save_rules_tests.cpp`
(`ctest` reports 3/3). They build as native binaries because they exercise
ABI-independent discovery, lifecycle, and configuration logic. Every
other test name in CMakeLists.txt is gated behind
`if(EXISTS tests/autocloud_native_tests.cpp)`, upstream's own private
tests/ directory that isn't part of this repo.

Built via `make ronin-module` (nix build .#cloud-redirect + stage into
module/payload/), the same target `make deploy-tsuki-module` and
`make rollback-tsuki-module` depend on.

