**Live acceptance, 2026-07-31 (RONIN-CLOUD-7, and a two-module test):** ran
a real two-module Tsuki session -- this package and `slssteam-ronin` both
active, injected into the same real 32-bit Steam process (via a NixOS
`bwrap`-sandboxed launch; `ubuntu12_32/steam`) simultaneously. Confirmed via
`/proc/<pid>/maps`: `cloud_redirect.so` (LD_PRELOAD) and
`SLSsteam.so`/`library-inject.so` (LD_AUDIT) all mapped into the same
process with no env-var collisions (required a namespacing fix in Tsuki's
`steamlaunchext.lua`, see [[tsuki_multi_launch_extension]] memory). Both
fully initialized. `$TSUKI_RONIN_RUNTIME_DIR_M636C6F75647265646972656374/ready.json` was
written with the real Steam PID -- the `runtime-file` evidence carrier
(RONIN-CLOUD-7) confirmed working against a live host. Found and fixed in
that pass: `Log::Init()` didn't read
`TSUKI_RONIN_LOG_FILE_M636C6F75647265646972656374`;
re-verified live in a follow-up session.

**Live acceptance (RONIN-CLOUD-1), same day, follow-up session:** with the
two-module session running, wrote a new `<appid>.lua` into
`<Steam>/config/stplug-in/` mid-session. Within one watch cycle:
`namespace app <id> (source: stplug-in)`, `1 new` -- discovery fires
without a restart. Stats-seeding correctly stayed off (no `config.json` ->
`sync_achievements`/`sync_playtime` default `false`) -- expected, not a gap.

**RONIN-CLOUD-4, tested via an isolated harness (no real Steam involved):**
every live session had resolved the `steamclient.so` poll on the first
check, so built a throwaway 32-bit process (named literally "steam" --
`OnLoad()`'s constructor gates on that name or an already-mapped
steamclient.so) that dlopen'd a fake stand-in `steamclient.so` 3 real
seconds after start. Precise timing proof: `waiting for steamclient.so` at
t=+0.000s, `starting` at t=+3.000s -- confirms the poll genuinely waits
across multiple ~500ms iterations, not an instant resolution, with zero
risk to any real Steam install. Found and fixed in the same pass:
`DebugLog()` had no `mkdir()` before its `open()` (unlike `Log::Init()`'s
default path), so on a genuinely fresh install (no prior
`~/.config/CloudRedirect/`) it failed closed with `ENOENT` and stayed
silent for the whole process. Reproduced and confirmed fixed with the same
harness technique, pristine scratch `$HOME`.
